VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key

# Server-only. Required by /api/email-data and by the email_logs write path in
# /api/send-email and /api/send-custom-email.
#
# WHY: 20260818000003_lock_pii_tables_and_policies_v3.sql revoked every
# privilege on `email_logs` and `email_sender_config` from `anon`, so anything
# touching those tables with the anon key now fails with 42501
# ("permission denied for table email_logs"). Never expose this key to the
# browser — it bypasses RLS.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_supabase_service_role_key

# ── Clerk (CoCo-Connect sign in / sign up) ───────────────────────────────────
# Both are optional. With no publishable key the auth screens keep using the
# original /api/auth email+password flow, so the site works either way.
#
# VITE_* is inlined into the browser bundle by Vite — publishable key only.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_your_publishable_key
#
# Server-only, never VITE_. Used by the `clerk-session` action in /api/auth to
# verify the session JWT before minting the marketplace cookie.
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_secret_key

# ── Analytics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The site uses a SELF-HOSTED analytics system (Supabase + Vercel), not a
# third-party script. No analytics key is required in the browser bundle.
#
#   src/lib/visitorTracking.ts          client tracker (sessions, clicks,
#                                       heatmaps, scroll, funnel, exit)
#   src/components/VisitorTracker.tsx  React mount
#   api/visitor-tracking.js            ingestion + dashboard queries
#   src/components/VisitorAnalyticsPanel.tsx  dashboard UI
#   supabase/migrations/20261105000001_create_visitor_tracking.sql  schema
#
# Requires the same SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY as the other API routes. Run the
# migration once in the Supabase SQL editor — Vercel does NOT auto-apply it.
#
# Country/region/city come from Vercel's x-vercel-ip-* request headers, so no
# GeoIP service or extra key is needed (works on deployed builds only).
#
# NOTE: Microsoft Clarity (src/lib/analytics.ts + AnalyticsTracker.tsx) is kept
# on disk but is NO LONGER MOUNTED in App.tsx. VITE_CLARITY_ID is intentionally
# unused — do not set it, or you would be paying for two trackers.

